<Doc lang={lang} page="blocks" current="Stars" title="Stars/background"
  description="The Stars/background block of FLOAT: a network takes the stars off the linear image, giving the starless image and the stars alone, which add up to the original; how Post uses them; the Synthetic stars block; settings and limits.">

  <p class="kicker">Block</p>
  <h1>Stars/background</h1>
  <p class="meta">FLOAT 0.2.0 · beta of {release.date.en}</p>

  <dl class="inshort"><div><dt>What it does</dt><dd>It separates the stars from the rest of the image, so that each can be stretched on its own.</dd></div><div><dt>What it shows</dt><dd>Two images, the starless image and the stars alone, which reach Post as one layer with its own star sliders.</dd></div><div><dt>What can be set</dt><dd>The block itself has no setting; in Post, Stars makes the stars brighter or fainter and Star size shrinks or grows them, and the defaults already tone them down a little.</dd></div></dl>

  <aside class="note toc">
    <b>On this page</b>
    <ol>
